Third-party material
--------------------
The MIT license above covers only the code and documentation written for this
project. Except as noted below, third-party code is not included in this
repository; it is fetched at build or install time and keeps its own license:
ESP-IDF, esp_codec_dev, esp_websocket_client, esp_hosted 2.12.6,
esp_wifi_remote 1.6.5, esp_lcd_ek79007 2.0.2, esp_lcd_jd9365 2.0.2, and
esp_lcd_st7701 2.0.2
(1.1.0 for ESP-IDF below 5.4; Apache License 2.0, Espressif Systems), plus the
Python packages listed in pyproject.toml (each under its own license).

Firmware images include libopus, Xiph.Org's Opus codec, built for ESP-IDF by the
esp-opus component (78/esp-opus 1.0.x,
https://components.espressif.com/components/78/esp-opus), fetched at build time
and used to decode Opus reply audio. libopus is under the BSD 3-Clause License,
Copyright 2001-2023 Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy
B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo,
Mozilla, Amazon. A copy of its license is in LICENSES/libopus-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
The Hermes plugin can load the host's own libopus at run time; none is
distributed with it.

Optional Linux audio uses python-sounddevice (MIT, Matthias Geier) and the
system PortAudio library (MIT). Raspberry Pi controls use GPIO Zero
(BSD-3-Clause) and the system lgpio library (Unlicense). These dependencies are
installed separately; their packages carry their respective license texts.
The optional Linux display uses pygame (LGPL 2.1) and SDL2 (zlib), also
installed separately. No pygame or SDL source is copied into this repository.

The optional MQTT example uses Eclipse Paho MQTT Python, dual licensed under
Eclipse Public License 2.0 and Eclipse Distribution License 1.0. It is installed
separately; its package includes both license texts. No Paho source is copied
into this repository.

