The T-Display-S3 ST7789 initialization values and AW9364 backlight control in
firmware/esp32/main/port_parallel.cpp follow Xinyuan-LilyGO's factory example,
https://github.com/Xinyuan-LilyGO/T-Display-S3/blob/ec889e789b3cf093412689a143f7f37b42b56af7/examples/factory/factory.ino,
Copyright (c) 2022 Xinyuan-LilyGO, MIT License.
The adapter uses ESP-IDF GPIO and panel APIs, bounds brightness to 16 levels,
protects pulse timing, and uses explicit microsecond delays for backlight reset
and startup. The panel command lengths are stored separately from their values.
The full upstream license is in LICENSES/LilyGO-MIT.txt.

The QMI8658 register facts in firmware/drivers/qmi8658.cpp (the WHO_AM_I
value, the soft-reset command and its 15 ms boot time, the control register
settings and the little-endian accelerometer data layout) come from QST's
QMI8658A datasheet Rev A,
https://qstcorp.com/upload/pdf/202301/13-52-25%20QMI8658A%20Datasheet%20Rev%20A.pdf,
Copyright (c) 2022 QST Corporation. Hardware facts only; no QST code is
included.

The PCF85063 register facts in firmware/drivers/pcf85063.cpp (the BCD time
registers 0x04-0x0A, the oscillator-stop flag on the seconds register and the
burst-write behavior that restarts the clock) come from NXP's PCF85063A
datasheet, https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/PCF85063A.pdf. Hardware
facts only; no NXP code is included.

The days_from_civil date conversion in firmware/drivers/pcf85063.cpp follows
Howard Hinnant's public-domain algorithm,
https://howardhinnant.github.io/date_algorithms.html#days_from_civil.

The QR code encoder in firmware/core/third_party/qrcode/ is vendored from
Richard Moore's QRCode library, https://github.com/ricmoo/QRCode,
revision eafbde494979abc2445c363cc2602230bcbe299c,
Copyright (c) 2017 Richard Moore and Copyright (c) 2017 Project Nayuki,
MIT License. Major parts derive from Project Nayuki's QR Code generator,
https://www.nayuki.io/page/qr-code-generator-library. The vendored copy is
adapted for this project: the C99 variable-length arrays are replaced with
fixed, bounded buffers so MSVC accepts the file; the "#pragma mark" lines are
replaced with comments; an always-false comparison is removed; and two bounds
checks are added (the bit writer no longer writes past its buffer, and a payload
that overflows the chosen version is rejected instead of encoded incorrectly).
The full upstream license is in LICENSES/QRCode-MIT.txt.


